nizational Unit (OU)**: department or unit."},"2212":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management-113","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management#generate-a-csr","content":"**Country (C)**: two-letter country code."},"2213":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management-114","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management#generate-a-csr","content":"**State / Province (ST)**: state or province."},"2214":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management-115","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management#generate-a-csr","content":"**Locality (L)**: city or locality."},"2215":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management-116","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management#generate-a-csr","content":"**Email Address**: contact email."},"2216":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management-117","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management#generate-a-csr","content":"**Subject Alternative Names (SANs)**: alternative names or identifiers, such as DNS or IP."},"2217":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management-118","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management#generate-a-csr","content":"Download the CSR and run `openssl req -in request.csr -noout -verify -text`. Check signature, subject and SAN before sending it. A CSR does not determine the final certificate by itself: issuance policy can replace its fields."},"2218":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management-119","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management#sign-locally-with-pkcs11","content":"Lamassu also offers specific help for local integrations through **Sign locally with OpenSSL & PKCS11 tools**."},"2219":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management-120","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management#sign-locally-with-pkcs11","content":"Requiere el módulo, token y permisos del proveedor correspondiente. Comprueba que el identificador de Lamassu se corresponde con el objeto accesible desde ese módulo. La configuración del módulo pertenece al entorno del cliente o al Despliegue."},"2220":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management-121","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/key-management#before-deleting-a-key","content":"Review **Related Entities** and locate CAs, certificates and validation processes that still need signatures. Revoking a CA does not remove the need to publish status during its retention period. Deleting a key does not automatically revoke its certificates either. Plan replacement and retention before using **Delete Key**; provider deletion behavior depends on the engine."},"2221":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","type":"page","content":"Online validation with OCSP","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","PKI","Validation"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp"},"2222":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-0","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","content":"Query signed status and verify the responder’s response."},"2223":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-1","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"How the responder works in Lamassu"},"2224":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-2","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#embedding-in-issued-certificates","content":"Embedding in issued certificates"},"2225":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-3","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"HTTP endpoints"},"2226":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-4","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#generate-and-verify-a-query","content":"Generate and verify a query"},"2227":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-5","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#check-from-the-interface","content":"Check from the interface"},"2228":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-6","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#references","content":"References"},"2229":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-7","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","content":"OCSP queries a certificate’s status and returns a signed response. This guide is for an integrator checking what Lamassu publishes and how the consumer must verify it. For complete identity validation, follow Certificate validation."},"2230":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-8","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"The responder retrieves the certificate by serial number and locates its issuing CA in the inventory. It translates persisted status as follows:"},"2231":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-9","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"Record status"},"2232":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-10","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"Signed response"},"2233":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-11","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"`ACTIVE`"},"2234":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-12","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"`Good`."},"2235":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-13","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"`REVOKED`"},"2236":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-14","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"`Revoked`, with revocation reason and timestamp."},"2237":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-15","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"Other states, including `INACTIVE` and `EXPIRED`"},"2238":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-16","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"`Unknown` if the certificate and issuer can be retrieved."},"2239":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-17","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"An absent serial number causes a lookup error; it does not guarantee a signed `Unknown` response. Lookup or signing errors produce an HTTP failure. Treat that as unavailable evidence according to consumer policy."},"2240":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-18","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"The issuing CA itself signs the response through its KMS-associated key. A delegated OCSP signing certificate is not used. An imported CA without a usable key cannot sign responses."},"2241":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-19","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"The implementation sets `thisUpdate` approximately one day before response generation and `nextUpdate` one day after: the declared window is about 48 hours. Inspect received values and apply your freshness policy. The response reflects stored status when queried; a previously cached copy does not change upon revocation."},"2242":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-20","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#embedding-in-issued-certificates","content":"The signer constructs OCSP URLs from configured VA domains and adds them to AIA. Without domains, there is no URL to add; an imported certificate retains its original extensions. Inspect the actual certificate:"},"2243":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-21","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#embedding-in-issued-certificates","content":"Check that the consumer can reach this URL. DNS, endpoint exposure and domain configuration belong to Deployment. Changing configuration does not modify already signed certificates."},"2244":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-22","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"The service accepts:"},"2245":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-23","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"Method"},"2246":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-24","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"VA service path"},"2247":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-25","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"Format"},"2248":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-26","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"`POST`"},"2249":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-27","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"`/ocsp`"},"2250":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-28","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"DER request, `Content-Type: application/ocsp-request`."},"2251":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-29","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"`GET`"},"2252":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-30","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"`/ocsp/{ocsp_request}`"},"2253":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-31","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"DER request encoded using padded URL Base64."},"2254":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-32","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"Use POST to avoid client encoding differences. A successful response has `Content-Type: application/ocsp-response` and a DER body. The public prefix depends on the Gateway; use the URL published in the certificate and checked by the operator."},"2255":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-33","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#generate-and-verify-a-query","content":"You need OpenSSL 3.x, `device.crt`, its direct issuer’s certificate `issuer.pem` and the consumer’s trusted roots in `roots.pem`. For an intermediate issuer, also prepare `intermediates.pem` containing the intermediate CAs."},"2256":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-34","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#generate-and-verify-a-query","content":"Generate the request:"},"2257":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-35","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#generate-and-verify-a-query","content":"This example omits the nonce because the responder does not echo it. Verification relies on signature, response correspondence and timestamps; it does not demonstrate freshness through a nonce."},"2258":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-36","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#generate-and-verify-a-query","content":"Replace the example URL with the inspected endpoint:"},"2259":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-37","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#generate-and-verify-a-query","content":"Verify the returned DER:"},"2260":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-38","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#generate-and-verify-a-query","content":"For intermediates, add `-verify_other intermediates.pem`. Require successful response verification and inspect the status corresponding to `device.crt`, issuer, serial, `thisUpdate` and `nextUpdate`. `Response verify OK` validates the response only: also observe `good`, `revoked` or `unknown`. Do not accept an identity based only on the command’s exit code."},"2261":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-39","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#check-from-the-interface","content":"**OCSP Check** shows what Lamassu returns for a selected certificate. Complete the check from the consumer’s network and trust store: a console query does not establish its validation configuration."},"2262":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-40","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#check-from-the-interface","content":"To check a change, save an earlier response, revoke a test certificate and request another response. The new query should reflect persisted status; compare timestamps to rule out reuse of an earlier response. If it fails, follow PKI troubleshooting."},"2263":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-41","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#references","content":"RFC 6960: OCSP."},"2264":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-42","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#references","content":"OpenSSL: openssl-ocsp."},"2265":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-43","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#references","content":"<Card title=\"CRL service\" href=\"/docs/platform/pki/crl\" />"},"2266":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp-44","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp#references","content":"<Card title=\"Certificate validation\" href=\"/docs/platform/pki/certificate-validation\" />"},"2267":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","type":"page","content":"PKI","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","PKI"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview"},"2268":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-0","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","content":"Administer keys and authorities, define issuance and verify the resulting certificates."},"2269":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-1","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#start-here","content":"Start here"},"2270":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-2","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#what-you-need","content":"What you need"},"2271":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-3","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#core-capabilities","content":"Core capabilities"},"2272":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-4","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#build-your-trust-hierarchy","content":"Build your trust hierarchy"},"2273":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-5","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#protect-cryptographic-keys","content":"Protect cryptographic keys"},"2274":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-6","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#issue-and-control-certificates","content":"Issue and control certificates"},"2275":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-7","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#publish-validation-status","content":"Publish validation status"},"2276":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-8","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#how-to-check-the-result","content":"How to check the result"},"2277":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-9","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#continue","content":"Continue"},"2278":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-10","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","content":"The PKI section explains how to build and operate X.509 trust in Lamassu: which authorities issue, which rules apply and how to check certificates. It is intended for PKI administrators and anyone who needs to use certificates in a consuming system."},"2279":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-11","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#start-here","content":"Follow PKI getting started to create a CA, issue a client certificate and verify it with OpenSSL. The result is a certificate, its private key and a verified chain."},"2280":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-12","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#start-here","content":"You can complete that path before managing devices. When you need to associate the identity with an inventory or automate its enrollment, continue in IoT Fleets."},"2281":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-13","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#what-you-need","content":"An accessible instance and permission to manage the keys, CAs and certificates you will use."},"2282":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-14","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#what-you-need","content":"An available cryptographic engine to keep the authority's key."},"2283":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-15","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#what-you-need","content":"The certificate's purpose, such as authenticating a client through mTLS."},"2284":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-16","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#what-you-need","content":"Consumer requirements: accepted issuers, algorithms, names and permitted usages."},"2285":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-17","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#what-you-need","content":"Prepare the instance and cryptographic provider in Deployment. The trust model explains hierarchy choices."},"2286":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-18","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#build-your-trust-hierarchy","content":"Authorities sign certificates. A root establishes the trust anchor, and an intermediate separates issuance by environment or purpose. Hierarchy and rotation explains how to maintain trust when replacing an authority."},"2287":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-19","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#protect-cryptographic-keys","content":"CA signing keys are managed through KMS and cryptographic engines. A client that generates a CSR can keep its own key: preserve that custody when choosing the issuance method."},"2288":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-20","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#issue-and-control-certificates","content":"A profile establishes subject, validity, usage and key restrictions. The CA applies issuance configuration and signs the certificate. In the inventory, you can inspect the result, download it and manage its status."},"2289":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-21","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#publish-validation-status","content":"Validation covers the chain, validity, usages and revocation status. Lamassu publishes status through OCSP and CRL; the consumer configures which issuers it recognizes and how it checks that status."},"2290":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-22","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#how-to-check-the-result","content":"An active certificate in the console is one part of the check. Also verify that:"},"2291":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-23","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#how-to-check-the-result","content":"its subject and extensions identify the expected client;"},"2292":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-24","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#how-to-check-the-result","content":"its public key matches the client's private key;"},"2293":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-25","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#how-to-check-the-result","content":"its chain reaches a root trusted by the consumer;"},"2294":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-26","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#how-to-check-the-result","content":"its dates and usages allow the operation;"},"2295":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-27","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#how-to-check-the-result","content":"the consumer applies revocation checks and authorization."},"2296":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-28","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#how-to-check-the-result","content":"The issuance path includes the first independent checks."},"2297":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-29","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#continue","content":"<Card title=\"PKI getting started\" description=\"Create a CA, then issue and verify a client certificate.\" href=\"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview\" />"},"2298":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-30","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#continue","content":"<Card title=\"Apply PKI to devices\" description=\"Associate certificates with inventory and prepare enrollment.\" href=\"/docs/platform/iot-fleets/overview\" />"},"2299":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview-31","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/overview#continue","content":"<Card title=\"PKI diagnostics\" description=\"Check issuance, OCSP and CRL when the result fails.\" href=\"/docs/platform/pki/troubleshooting\" />"},"2300":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","type":"page","content":"Create your first CA","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","PKI","Getting started"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority"},"2301":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-0","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","content":"Create an evaluation root and check its certificate before issuing."},"2302":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-1","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#before-you-begin","content":"Before you begin"},"2303":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-2","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#open-the-creation-wizard-toc","content":"Open the creation wizard [!toc]"},"2304":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-3","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#select-the-key-toc","content":"Select the key [!toc]"},"2305":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-4","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#define-the-authority-toc","content":"Define the authority [!toc]"},"2306":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-5","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#review-and-create-the-ca-toc","content":"Review and create the CA [!toc]"},"2307":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-6","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#verify-the-result-toc","content":"Verify the result [!toc]"},"2308":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-7","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#check-the-ca-certificate","content":"Check the CA certificate"},"2309":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-8","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#if-the-result-fails","content":"If the result fails"},"2310":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-9","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#next-step","content":"Next step"},"2311":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-10","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","content":"You will create a root authority with a new key kept by a Lamassu engine. The result is an active CA and its public certificate in `ca.pem`, ready to verify issuance in the next path."},"2312":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-11","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#before-you-begin","content":"Console access and permission to create keys and authorities."},"2313":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-12","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#before-you-begin","content":"An available cryptographic engine that supports the chosen algorithm."},"2314":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-13","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#before-you-begin","content":"OpenSSL 3.x to check the downloaded certificate."},"2315":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-14","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#before-you-begin","content":"Use an evaluation instance or an authority intended for these tests. The example creates a root that issues directly; to design an operational hierarchy, see Hierarchy and rotation."},"2316":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-15","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#open-the-creation-wizard-toc","content":"In **Certification Authorities**, select **Create New CA** and choose to create a CA with a new key pair."},"2317":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-16","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#open-the-creation-wizard-toc","content":"The &#x2A;*Create New CA (Existing Key)** flow is explained in the authorities guide."},"2318":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-17","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#select-the-key-toc","content":"Choose the engine that will keep the key and an algorithm its capabilities allow. For this example, you can use **EC P-384** if available."},"2319":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-18","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#select-the-key-toc","content":"The CA private key is used through the engine. In this path, you will download only the authority's public certificate."},"2320":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-19","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#define-the-authority-toc","content":"Select **Root CA** and complete:"},"2321":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-20","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#define-the-authority-toc","content":"**CA Name**: `Acme Evaluation Root CA`."},"2322":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-21","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#define-the-authority-toc","content":"**Subject**: organization and country details for your evaluation."},"2323":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-22","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#define-the-authority-toc","content":"**CA Certificate Expiration**: for example, one year from creation."},"2324":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-23","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#define-the-authority-toc","content":"**Default End-Entity Certificate Issuance Expiration**: for example, 90 days, within the CA's lifetime."},"2325":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-24","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#define-the-authority-toc","content":"The CA name becomes its `Common Name`. Keep the CA usages needed to sign certificates and CRLs."},"2326":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-25","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#review-and-create-the-ca-toc","content":"Check the engine, algorithm, subject, root type and dates. Confirm creation and note the authority identifier so you can recognize it in the DMS or API."},"2327":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-26","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#verify-the-result-toc","content":"Open the new CA. It should appear active, show its certificate and allow access to **Issued Certificates**."},"2328":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-27","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#verify-the-result-toc","content":"Download or copy the authority's PEM certificate and save it as `ca.pem`. Check that the file contains the complete block, including `BEGIN CERTIFICATE` and `END CERTIFICATE`."},"2329":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-28","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#check-the-ca-certificate","content":"Run from the directory where you saved `ca.pem`:"},"2330":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-29","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#check-the-ca-certificate","content":"Check that the subject and issuer match the root you created, the dates include the current time, **Basic Constraints** contains `CA:TRUE` and **Key Usage** allows certificate signing. The last command should return `ca.pem: OK`."},"2331":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-30","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#check-the-ca-certificate","content":"You explicitly selected `ca.pem` as the trust anchor for this test. A valid self-signature does not install that trust in other consumers. See the openssl-verify reference for verification options."},"2332":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-31","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#if-the-result-fails","content":"If creation fails, check permissions, engine availability and the selected algorithm."},"2333":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-32","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#if-the-result-fails","content":"If OpenSSL cannot read the file, copy the complete PEM block again."},"2334":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-33","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#if-the-result-fails","content":"If signature or date checks fail, check that you downloaded this CA's certificate and that your computer's clock is correct."},"2335":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-34","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#if-the-result-fails","content":"PKI diagnostics covers issuance checks and cryptographic dependencies."},"2336":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority-35","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority#next-step","content":"Continue with Issue and verify a certificate, using this authority and `ca.pem`."},"2337":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","type":"page","content":"Issue and verify a certificate","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","PKI","Getting started"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate"},"2338":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-0","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","content":"Issue a client certificate and check content, chain and key correspondence."},"2339":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-1","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#before-you-begin","content":"Before you begin"},"2340":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-2","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#start-the-issuance","content":"Start the issuance"},"2341":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-3","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#choose-the-method","content":"Choose the method"},"2342":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-4","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#identify-the-certificate","content":"Identify the certificate"},"2343":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-5","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#configure-key-and-uses","content":"Configure key and uses"},"2344":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-6","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#issue-and-download","content":"Issue and download"},"2345":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-7","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#verify-the-result","content":"Verify the result"},"2346":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-8","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#inspect-content-and-dates","content":"Inspect content and dates"},"2347":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-9","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#verify-the-chain","content":"Verify the chain"},"2348":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-10","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#check-that-the-key-matches","content":"Check that the key matches"},"2349":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-11","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#if-the-result-fails","content":"If the result fails"},"2350":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-12","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#next-step","content":"Next step"},"2351":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-13","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","content":"You will issue an end-entity certificate for `device-001` using browser key and CSR generation. The result is `device.crt`, `device.key` and the issuing root's public certificate, `ca.pem`."},"2352":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-14","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#before-you-begin","content":"An active root CA with an available signing key and permission to issue. If one does not exist yet, follow Create your first CA."},"2353":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-15","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#before-you-begin","content":"Its public certificate in `ca.pem`; this example uses the root created in the previous path."},"2354":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-16","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#before-you-begin","content":"OpenSSL 3.x and a working directory with restricted access."},"2355":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-17","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#before-you-begin","content":"A client identifier: here we use `device-001`."},"2356":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-18","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#before-you-begin","content":"In this flow, the client's key is generated in the browser and must be downloaded when issuance finishes. If you lose it, you must generate a key and issue another certificate. The certificate inventory lets you download the public certificate, but cannot recover this key."},"2357":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-19","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#start-the-issuance","content":"Open the CA from the previous path, go to **Issued Certificates** and select **Issue New**."},"2358":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-20","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#choose-the-method","content":"Select **Generate Key & CSR in Browser** to follow this example."},"2359":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-21","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#choose-the-method","content":"If the key must be generated and kept on the destination system, use **Upload Existing CSR**, described in the authorities guide."},"2360":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-22","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#identify-the-certificate","content":"Enter `device-001` as the `Common Name`. Add subject details required by your policy and SANs if the consumer uses them to identify the client."},"2361":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-23","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#identify-the-certificate","content":"If you continue with manual registration, the `Device ID` will be exactly `device-001`."},"2362":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-24","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#configure-key-and-uses","content":"Choose an algorithm and size allowed by the profile; for example, ECDSA P-256 if permitted. For this client certificate, select **Digital Signature** and **Client Authentication**, and issue it as an end-entity certificate."},"2363":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-25","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#configure-key-and-uses","content":"Request, for example, 30 days of validity, always within the CA's lifetime. Review the issuance profile if the resulting content differs from the request."},"2364":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-26","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#issue-and-download","content":"Confirm issuance. Save the PEM certificate as `device.crt` and the private key as `device.key` in your prepared directory."},"2365":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-27","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#verify-the-result","content":"Check in **Issued Certificates** that the certificate appears active. Note its serial number and verify the downloaded material using the checks below."},"2366":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-28","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#inspect-content-and-dates","content":"Check `CN=device-001`, the expected issuer, current validity, **Digital Signature** and the extended usage **TLS Web Client Authentication**. It must be an end-entity certificate: it must not declare `CA:TRUE` or enable **Certificate Sign**. If **Basic Constraints** is present, it must indicate `CA:FALSE`. If you requested SANs, check that the expected identifiers appear in the certificate."},"2367":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-29","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#verify-the-chain","content":"The expected result is `device.crt: OK`. This check uses your explicit root and evaluates the chain, dates and compatibility with the TLS client purpose. Also check for the expected usages and names through the inspection above."},"2368":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-30","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#verify-the-chain","content":"If you use an intermediate CA, the trusted root must be in `ca.pem` and you must supply the intermediates with `-untrusted intermediates.pem`. This variant is covered in the trust model."},"2369":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-31","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#verify-the-chain","content":"The command does not query OCSP or CRL. For revocation checks, continue with Certificate validation. See the openssl-verify reference for its options."},"2370":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-32","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#check-that-the-key-matches","content":"In Bash, compare the two public-key digests:"},"2371":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-33","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#check-that-the-key-matches","content":"Both commands must finish successfully and show the same SHA-256 digest. If they differ, the private key does not match the selected certificate. Find the correct pair before installing it."},"2372":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-34","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#check-that-the-key-matches","content":"The options used are documented in openssl-x509 and openssl-pkey."},"2373":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-35","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#if-the-result-fails","content":"Result"},"2374":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-36","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#if-the-result-fails","content":"What to review"},"2375":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-37","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#if-the-result-fails","content":"The CA rejects issuance"},"2376":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-38","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#if-the-result-fails","content":"Permissions, CA state and key, algorithm and profile."},"2377":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-39","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#if-the-result-fails","content":"Different subject or usages"},"2378":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-40","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#if-the-result-fails","content":"Applied profile and requested values."},"2379":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-41","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#if-the-result-fails","content":"Issuer cannot be found"},"2380":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-42","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#if-the-result-fails","content":"Downloaded CA and required intermediate chain."},"2381":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-43","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#if-the-result-fails","content":"Validity fails"},"2382":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-44","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#if-the-result-fails","content":"Certificate and CA dates, and the computer's clock."},"2383":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-45","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#if-the-result-fails","content":"Public-key digests differ"},"2384":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-46","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#if-the-result-fails","content":"Certificate and key files from the same issuance."},"2385":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-47","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#if-the-result-fails","content":"See PKI diagnostics to narrow an issuance failure."},"2386":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-48","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#next-step","content":"You have completed the PKI path when the certificate verifies and the key matches. Choose how to use it:"},"2387":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-49","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#next-step","content":"Manage certificates for inspection, status and revocation."},"2388":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-50","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#next-step","content":"Register a device manually to associate this identity with Lamassu's inventory."},"2389":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-51","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#next-step","content":"Prepare ES