[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview","content":"This path is intended for those starting to administer PKI or needing a first X.509 client identity. It ends with three files: a root CA certificate, an end-entity certificate and the client's private key."},"2398":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview-6","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview#before-you-begin","content":"A Lamassu instance accessible from your browser. To prepare one, see Deployment."},"2399":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview-7","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview#before-you-begin","content":"Permission to manage keys, authorities and issuance. See Access control if an operation is blocked."},"2400":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview-8","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview#before-you-begin","content":"An available cryptographic engine for the CA key; check the keys and engines inventory."},"2401":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview-9","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview#before-you-begin","content":"OpenSSL 3.x on the computer where you will verify the files."},"2402":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview-10","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview#before-you-begin","content":"A working directory with restricted access for the downloaded key."},"2403":{"id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview-11","page_id":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview#recommended-path","content":"<Card title=\"1. Create your first CA\" description=\