vate key."],[770,"**Validation Authority (VA).** Publishes the status of certificates through OCSP and CRL."],[1995,"**Validation CAs:** authenticate the client certificates used for enrollment or migration. During re-enrollment, the enrollment CA is always trusted and Lamassu then tries the validation CAs configured in the re-enrollment block; those are optional."],[691,"**Validation:** `va.role.crl.create`."],[2152,"**View Details** to inspect metadata, identifiers and relationships."],[2694,"**Webhook delivery.** One enroll or re-enroll through each migrated webhook completes its authorization call."],[1102,"**Webhook:** useful when another authority knows inventory, credentials or entitlement to a requested ID."],[653,"**Webhook** delivers the event to an automation, SIEM or incident system via `POST` or `PUT`."],[2625,"**Webhooks with file references.** A mixed config, with a PEM certificate and a file-path key, is migrated to `mtls_options.cert_file` and `mtls_options.key_file`. Webhook delivery rejects those fields on every call, whatever the configured authentication mode, so every enroll and re-enroll that calls that webhook fails until the config is fixed. If the webhook uses mTLS, re-enter the certificate and key as Base64-encoded or plain PEM; if it does not, remove the leftover file fields. Metadata-only updates keep working in the meantime (`PUT` or `PATCH` on `/v1/dms/:id/metadata`). In a variant of the same problem, a stored config with file paths inside `mtls_options.cert_content` or `mtls_options.key_content` makes every full settings update (`POST /v1/dms` or `PUT /v1/dms/:id`) fail validation; settings are replaced wholesale, so resend the config with the certificate and key as PEM."],[2692,"**Webhooks without file fields.** For each DMS that uses a webhook for enrollment or re-enrollment, the `config` block carries `insecure_skip_verify` and the expected option block (`apikey_options`, `jwt_options` or `mtls_options`), with the certificate and k