nd that your computer's clock is correct."],[2639,"If the deployment runs on SQLite, `couch_db` or `dynamo_db`, move it to PostgreSQL first."],[2656,"If the deployment uses local KMS or VA storage, those pods fail until you complete step 4, so `--wait` cannot succeed: Helm waits for them to become ready, times out, exits with an error and marks the release `failed`. The hooks have already run by then, and every manifest, including the new StatefulSets and their PVCs, has been applied. Helm does not roll anything back without `--atomic`. Continue with step 4, then re-run the same `helm upgrade` command so it completes and Helm records the release as `deployed`. Both hooks are idempotent, so they are safe to run again."],[2049,"If the first CA is deleted, CRL generation for the remaining one fails because the configured signer no longer matches a CA with that name. Until the role’s signer is updated to a certificate of the remaining CA, the last published list keeps being served until it expires (7 days by default)."],[1946,"If the identity stops being trustworthy, Lamassu records the reason and time of revocation. OCSP and CRLs let consumers learn that status."],[2359,"If the key must be generated and kept on the destination system, use **Upload Existing CSR**, described in the authorities guide."],[2157,"If the key will be born inside Lamassu, the recommended flow is to generate a new pair managed directly by one of the configured engines."],[964,"If the previous certificate is ACTIVE, attempts Superseded revocation before binding its successor."],[1132,"If the previous identity is already revoked, retaining its files does not restore a valid connection. Recovery requires an admitted credential and authorized intervention according to the situation."],[1562,"If the result fails"],[2309,"If the result fails"],[2349,"If the result fails"],[516,"If the route declares constraints, it compares request data with the normalized attributes of the same principal contributing